{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>After he had struck.</b> After the Holy One, blessed be He, bestowed upon Israel all this goodness — that through him He struck Sihon and Og before them and dispossessed them of their land — after that He came to reprove them." "<b>Who dwelt in Ashtarot in Edrei.</b> We find three things called עשתרות in Scripture, and they are: mountains, flocks, and idolatry. The mountains — as mentioned here, אשר יושב בעשתרות, for just as Og king of Bashan was a great and mighty giant, strong as oaks, so too the place of his dwelling was fortified in high mountains; and this is עשתרות קרנים, which Scripture mentions (Genesis 14:5): ״ויכו את רפאים בעשתרות קרנים״; and it is called עשתרות קרנים because the flocks that have horns ascend there in those mountains, such as the wild goats, the goats, and the sheep. The flocks — as written (Deuteronomy 7:13): ״עשתרות צאנך״, for flocks of sheep are called עשתרות because they enrich their owners with wool, milk, and lambs; and they said in tractate Ḥullin: a person should always sell a field and acquire he-goats, as it is said (Proverbs 27:26–27): ״ומחיר שדה עתודים״, and it is written (ibid.): ״ודי חלב עזים ללחמך ללחם ביתך וחיים לנערותיך״. Idolatry — as written (Judges 10:6): ״ויעבדו את הבעלים ואת העשתרות״, for that idolatrous image was fashioned in the shape of a sheep." "<b>In Edrei.</b> The name of the province where the capital of the king was. They built it at the foot of the mountain on the plain, and there he gathered his entire camp, in the manner of what is written (Numbers 21:33): ״ויצא עוג מלך הבשן לקראתם הוא וכל עמו למלחמה אדרעי״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "In the Proverbs citation, the commentator reads ומחיר שדה עתודים whereas the standard text is ועזים עלי שדה; followed the commentator's reading as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:34.784731836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}